Encryption Model
   - AES-GCM (Advanced Encryption Standard - Galois/Counter Mode) with 256-bit keys
   - Client-side encryption using Web Crypto API before files are uploaded
   - End-to-end encryption where files are encrypted in the browser before being sent to the server
   - Separate encryption keys stored and shared with authorized doctors through the access control system
   - Session-based key management for temporary access

  Tech Stack
   - Frontend: React with TypeScript, Vite build tool
   - UI Components: shadcn/ui with Tailwind CSS
   - Styling: Tailwind CSS with dark/light theme support
   - Backend: Node.js with Express.js
   - Database: MongoDB with Mongoose ODM
   - File Storage: Local file system (uploads directory)
   - Authentication: JWT tokens with bcrypt for password hashing
   - API Communication: Axios for HTTP requests
   - State Management: React hooks and localStorage for session management
   - Build Tools: pnpm (as specified in package.json)
   - Additional APIs: Google Gemini AI for medical record analysis
